 return domain
```
This function uses the `urlparse` function from the `urllib.parse` module to parse the URL into its components. Then, it extracts the domain name from the `netloc` component of the parsed URL, splits it by dot and takes the last two elements. Finally, it concatenates those two elements with a dot to get the final domain name.
